      "name": null,
      "problem": "Solve $f(u)=0$ where $f(u)=\\frac{6{u}^{2}+6u-36}{3{u}^{2}+9u}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(u) & =\\frac{6{u}^{2}+6u-36}{3{u}^{2}+9u} \\\\  & =\\frac{6({u}^{2}+u-6)}{3u(u+3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{6(u+3)(u-2)}{3u(u+3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot \\cancel{3(u+3)}(u-2)}{u\\cdot \\cancel{3(u+3)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(u-2)}{u}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $u:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(u-2) & =0\\,⟹\\,u=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to $f(u)=0$ is $u=2.$",
